#
# Tepna — fold the box nights the corpus does not hold yet (E12,
# briefs/NIGHT-0928-ERRORS-2026-09-29-BRIEF.md). Measured 2026-09-29: nothing folded a box night
# automatically, the newest folded night was 2026-09-21, and the backlog was SEVEN nights —
# `tepna-nightly-triage` runs only the mutation crawl. A backlog is not a neutral state: a night that is
# not folded is a night whose QC, hat and trio numbers nobody can read.
#
# 🔴 NO NEW TOOL. `tools/trio-batch.mjs --skip-existing` IS the "fold only what is due" decider — its
# `redoReason` is a pure function returning why a night must be recomputed (no stamp, `inputs changed`,
# `code changed`) or null when skipping is provably safe, and the tool already emits ONE
# tepna.verdict/1 and persists it as `uploads/trio/trio-batch-verdicts.json`. A second decider would be a
# second definition of "due", free to drift from the one the fold uses. This unit is a SCHEDULE plus the
# handoff below, and nothing else.
#
# 🔴 A FOLD IS GIT-VISIBLE, AND THIS UNIT WAS WRITTEN ONCE ON THE OPPOSITE PREMISE. `.gitignore` has
# `uploads/*` at :16 and **`!uploads/trio/**` at :149** — trio folds are the one allowed addition under
# `uploads/` (owner, 2026-09-24) — so `git check-ignore` matches NOTHING for a fold path and 658
# `uploads/trio` files are tracked today. I read :16, concluded "a fold produces no file git can see",
# and said so; measuring the negation is what corrected it. So the fold's output is a COMMIT someone
# owes, not a byproduct.
#
# WHERE IT LANDS, AND WHY NOT THE PRIMARY CHECKOUT. `--out` is fixed to `uploads/trio` INSIDE this
# timer's own working directory and is deliberately NOT an environment variable: there must be no way to
# configure it into a checkout that sessions edit. A fold writes hundreds of megabytes across hundreds of
# files, and dropping that into the primary tree would dirty a tree nobody agreed to share (CLAUDE.md
# §2) and leave a session to discover it.
#
# IT COMMITS LOCALLY AND NEVER PUSHES. After a fold that changed something, the unit puts the result on a
# dated branch in its own checkout — staged BY EXPLICIT PATH (`git add -- uploads/trio`, never a blanket
# add) — so a session can relay it as a PR the next morning. Nothing leaves the machine: no push, no
# remote write, no credential needed. A run that changed nothing commits nothing, because an empty commit
# would be noise and a failed `git commit` would red the unit for doing its job.
#
# Only FOLD_SRC comes from the owner's EnvironmentFile: the captures root is the one path that must not
# appear in the repo. N-of-1 results stay off GitHub until a human relays them.
#
# INSTALL — the corpus machine only, and NOT performed by the PR that adds this file:
#   1. give the timer its OWN worktree at ~/wt-fold-timer (nobody edits there) and symlink
#      ~/Tepna/node_modules into it;
#   2. mkdir -p ~/.config/tepna and write fold.env with FOLD_SRC=<the captures root>;
#   3. cp tools/systemd/tepna-trio-fold.{service,timer} ~/.config/systemd/user/
#      systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user enable --now tepna-trio-fold.timer
#      systemctl --user list-timers tepna-trio-fold.timer      # the one-line check
# A separate checkout from the release and tchref timers' means no two timers race one detach, and
# because nobody edits there, re-pointing it at origin/main before each tick is safe.
[Unit]
Description=Tepna — fold the box nights the corpus does not hold yet
Documentation=https://github.com/Plantucha/Tepna/blob/main/tools/trio-batch.mjs

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/wt-fold-timer
EnvironmentFile=%h/.config/tepna/fold.env
ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/git fetch -q origin main
# Detach onto main before folding, so a fold branch left by the previous tick is never built upon: each
# run's commit sits on origin/main alone and is reviewable as one diff.
ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/git switch -q --detach origin/main
# A missing tool is "not on main yet", exit 0 — NOT a green verdict: nothing is written, so the previous
# verdict file keeps its own `at` stamp and reads as stale rather than as a pass. A missing or wrong
# FOLD_SRC is exit 2, a refusal, because a fold pointed at the wrong root writes a corpus nobody reads.
# ⚠️ NEVER add `--jobs`: forcing the fold's parallelism is a standing fleet rule. The tool sizes itself
# against the box; a fixed count either starves peers' gates or overruns memory.
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c '[ -f tools/trio-batch.mjs ] || { echo "trio-batch.mjs not on origin/main yet — nothing to run"; exit 0; }; [ -n "$FOLD_SRC" ] && [ -d "$FOLD_SRC" ] || { echo "fold.env: FOLD_SRC missing or not a directory ($FOLD_SRC)"; exit 2; }; node tools/trio-batch.mjs --src "$FOLD_SRC" --out uploads/trio --skip-existing --json'
# 🔴 THE TRIPWIRE, BEFORE THE HANDOFF. `uploads/*` ignores the `uploads/trio` DIRECTORY and
# `!uploads/trio/**` un-ignores its children — but git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the
# negation reaches those children only while something in there is ALREADY TRACKED. Measured in a scratch
# repo carrying those exact two lines with nothing tracked: `git status --porcelain -- uploads/trio` is
# EMPTY after a fold has written files, and `git add -- uploads/trio` is refused outright. Both work in
# this checkout only because main tracks 658 files there.
#
# So the handoff's own guard is NOT self-validating: "git sees no change" means EITHER nothing was folded
# OR git has gone blind to the whole directory, and those two must never share an exit code. A silent
# no-op every night is exactly how a fold backlog returns unnoticed — the defect E12 exists to end.
#
# ⚠️ KEYED ON TRACKEDNESS, NOT ON "the fold reported work", and deliberately: the run verdict carries no
# count of nights RECOMPUTED this tick (`folded` counts every PASS night, skipped ones included), so a
# tripwire reading it would fire on every all-skipped night and red the timer for working correctly.
# Trackedness is the condition that actually has to hold, it cannot be flaky, and it fires even on a tick
# that folded nothing — before the breakage can hide behind a quiet run.
ExecStartPost=/bin/sh -c 'test -n "$(git ls-files uploads/trio | head -1)" || { echo "REFUSING: uploads/trio is fully untracked here, so git cannot see a fold under it — uploads/* ignores the directory and !uploads/trio/** cannot reach into an ignored dir with nothing tracked. A commit would silently stage nothing. Restore the tracked fold tree before enabling this timer."; exit 2; }'
# The handoff. Separate from the fold so a fold that succeeded is never undone by a bookkeeping failure,
# and guarded on there being a change at all — reached only once the tripwire above has proved git can see
# the directory, so this exit 0 means "nothing was folded" and nothing else.
ExecStartPost=/bin/sh -c 'test -n "$(git status --porcelain -- uploads/trio)" || { echo "fold changed nothing under uploads/trio — no commit owed"; exit 0; }; b="fold/$(date +%%Y-%%m-%%d-%%H%%M)"; git switch -q -c "$b" && git add -- uploads/trio && git -c user.name="Tepna fold timer" -c user.email="fold-timer@localhost" commit -q -m "fold: nights folded $(date +%%Y-%%m-%%d) by tepna-trio-fold" -m "Unattended fold, LOCAL ONLY — this commit has never been pushed and the unit holds no credential. Relay it as a PR after reading the run verdict in uploads/trio/trio-batch-verdicts.json." -m "Fleet-Session: fold-timer" && echo "fold committed on $b — not pushed; relay it when a session reads the verdict"'
